The same session id is seeded twice — once under the `$HOME`-derived default root, once under a
cwd-rooted tree — with different numbers in each. Asserting the cwd numbers is what proves
`--projects-root` overrides the default rather than merely supplementing it.

Arithmetic, cwd transcript: one turn, 10:00:00 → 10:11:00 = 660s = 11 minutes. Tokens are the single
assistant line's `usage`: input 7, output 3, no cache fields = 0.
The home transcript would have given 6 minutes and input 10 / output 5, and must not appear.

-- fixtures/home/.claude/projects/proj-home/s-dual.jsonl --
{"type":"system","subtype":"init","timestamp":"2026-08-01T09:59:00.000Z"}
{"type":"user","isSidechain":false,"origin":{"kind":"human"},"timestamp":"2026-08-01T10:00:00.000Z","message":{"role":"user","content":"go"}}
{"type":"assistant","isSidechain":false,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T10:06:00.000Z","message":{"role":"assistant","model":"claude-home-1","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ok"}],"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"output_tokens":5}}}
-- fixtures/cwd/transcripts/proj-cwd/s-dual.jsonl --
{"type":"system","subtype":"init","timestamp":"2026-08-01T09:59:00.000Z"}
{"type":"user","isSidechain":false,"origin":{"kind":"human"},"timestamp":"2026-08-01T10:00:00.000Z","message":{"role":"user","content":"go"}}
{"type":"assistant","isSidechain":false,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T10:11:00.000Z","message":{"role":"assistant","model":"claude-cwd-1","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ok"}],"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"output_tokens":3}}}
-- fixtures/cwd/plan/index.md --
---
sessions:
- s-dual
---

Body.
-- cmd --
booping session-stats plan/index.md --projects-root transcripts --dry-run
